thinking_content: '**Formulating an Approach to the Sokoban Challenge**


  Okay, so I''ve got this RL on Sokoban task to tackle. It''s focused on planning-heavy tasks, and the goal is to leverage Ray for distributed parallel training.  I need to pick a track: agent architecture or RL algorithm improvement. Interesting. This seems like a fairly standard RL problem at first glance, but with the added complexity of the Sokoban domain.


  My initial thoughts are that I''m going to want to understand this environment well. It''s an 8x8 grid with boxes and targets, four discrete actions, and that 8x8x8 observation space with one-hot encoding sounds pretty standard. The rewards are also straightforward - success and box movements.


  The submission is based around defining hyperparameters, the network, the training step, optimizer and base seed. And I''ll need to do it using Ray, with four parallel seeds, hyperparameter sampling, and the final score will be the mean solve rate. That''s a good evaluation metric, I can immediately see the benefits of that - very useful.


