    I will now read `defaults.py` to understand the default implementations of various components and the hyperparameter ranges. This will complete my understanding of the system''s training framework.I have read `train_single.py`. This script is crucial for understanding the overall training process, including how trajectories are collected, actions are selected, and how RNN states are managed during rollouts and between updates. The explicit handling of `rnn_state` confirms that recurrent architectures are fully supported.


