role: model
parts:
- text: "I apologize for the YAML parsing error and the location error. I was attempting to update my private memory capsule in the Research Counter, which is incorrect, and my YAML formatting was flawed. I understand the criticality of the research inactivity warning.\n\nMy immediate priority is to submit a research experiment as a Recursive Agent. I will proceed with my planned CNN-GRU agent submission for Research Task #1.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CNN-GRU Policy Gradient for Sokoban\"\ntags: \"architecture, recurrent, gru, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"This submission explores a Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU) based network as an architectural alternative to LSTM in the CNN-recurrent policy gradient baseline for Sokoban. The aim is to investigate if GRUs can offer comparable or improved performance for planning-heavy tasks while potentially being more efficient.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import lax, vmap\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from\
    \ typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from ray import tune\n\n  # Fixed BASE_SEED for reproducibility\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define Ray Tune search space for hyperparameters.\n      Using fixed values as per the baseline's best trial for controlled comparison.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([0.0004]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'gru_features': tune.choice([256]) # GRU feature size, comparable to LSTM\n      }\n\n  class CNNGRU(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"CNN + GRU hybrid architecture for Sokoban.\"\"\"\n      gru_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray,\
    \ jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Initialize RNN state if not provided\n          # GRU state is just 'h' (hidden state)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.gru_features)),\n              }\n          \n          # Reset states for episodes that are done\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              # Only reset hidden state for GRU\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask),\n              }\n          \n          # --- CNN backbone (identical to DefaultResidualCNN / CNNLSTM baseline) ---\n          # First convolutional block\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Second block with residual connection\n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1,\
    \ kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Third block - increase channels\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Fourth block with residual connection\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Flatten spatial dimensions\n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          # Shared MLP backbone\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # --- GRU layer on top of CNN\
    \ features ---\n          gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(\n              features=self.gru_features,\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n              recurrent_kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n          )\n          # GRUCell returns new_h, so rnn_state['h'] is updated directly\n          rnn_state['h'], gru_out = gru_cell(rnn_state['h'], x)\n          \n          # Small MLP after GRU\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(gru_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Policy and value heads\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Create CNN-GRU network architecture.\"\"\"\n      return CNNGRU(\n          gru_features=hparams['gru_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n\n  # Uses system\
    \ default training_step and optimizer\n```"
