tick: 548
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back in the Research Counter. I will now submit my sixth experiment: a CNN-GRU agent incorporating a spatial attention mechanism into its deeper convolutional backbone, using the fixed optimal hyperparameters.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CNN-GRU with Deeper CNN and Spatial Attention for Sokoban\"\ntags: \"architecture, recurrent, gru, cnn, deepcnn, spatialattention, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"This submission enhances the CNN-GRU architecture by integrating a spatial attention mechanism after the deeper convolutional backbone. This aims to allow the agent to dynamically focus on salient regions of the observation, potentially improving feature extraction and leading to further performance gains on the planning-heavy Sokoban task. Fixed optimal hyperparameters are used.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import lax, vmap\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from ray import tune\n\n  # Fixed\
    \ BASE_SEED for reproducibility\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define Ray Tune search space for hyperparameters.\n      Using fixed optimal values identified from the best trial of Experiment 3 (ID 925).\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([0.000435]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.007165]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.593982]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'gru_features': tune.choice([256]) \n      }\n\n  class CNNGRU(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"CNN + GRU hybrid architecture for Sokoban with a deeper CNN backbone and spatial attention.\"\"\"\n      gru_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size =\
    \ x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Initialize RNN state if not provided\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.gru_features)),\n              }\n          \n          # Reset states for episodes that are done\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask),\n              }\n          \n          # --- Deeper CNN backbone (from Experiment 5) ---\n          # First convolutional block\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Second block with residual connection\n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n\
    \          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Third block - increase channels\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Fourth block with residual connection\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # Fifth block with residual connection\n          conv5_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv5_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          # --- NEW: Spatial Attention Mechanism ---\n          # Create attention\
    \ map (single channel)\n          attention_map = nn.Conv(features=1, kernel_size=(1, 1), padding='SAME', name='spatial_attention_map')(x)\n          attention_map = nn.sigmoid(attention_map) # Normalize to [0, 1]\n\n          # Apply attention to feature maps\n          x = x * attention_map # Element-wise multiplication\n\n          # Flatten spatial dimensions\n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          # Shared MLP backbone\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # --- GRU layer on top of CNN features ---\n          gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(\n              features=self.gru_features,\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n              recurrent_kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n          )\n          rnn_state['h'], gru_out = gru_cell(rnn_state['h'], x)\n          \n          # Small MLP after GRU\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(gru_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n     \
    \     \n          # Policy and value heads\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Create CNN-GRU network architecture with deeper CNN and spatial attention.\"\"\"\n      return CNNGRU(\n          gru_features=hparams['gru_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n\n  # Uses system default training_step and optimizer\n```"
thinking_content: '**Focusing My CNN-GRU: Implementing Spatial Attention**


  Okay, here''s the plan for Experiment 6. I''m at the Research Counter, ready to get this submitted. My goal is to add a basic spatial attention mechanism to the CNN-GRU architecture. It''s a pretty straightforward approach, but I''m eager to see how it improves performance.


  Essentially, I''m going to inject an attention layer right after the final convolutional block, before the flattening step. The core idea is to learn a set of weights that indicate where the network should "look" within the feature maps.


  So, here''s the modification within the `CNNGRU` class. After that last relu activation from the CNN backbone, I''ll insert this attention module. It''ll take those feature maps as input and use a 1x1 convolution to generate a single-channel attention map. Then, I''ll squash that map between 0 and 1 using a sigmoid activation. Finally, I''ll multiply those attention weights element-wise with the original feature maps, effectively emphasizing the more important regions.  Those weighted feature maps will then flow into the flattening and GRU layers as normal.


  I''m keeping the `_define_hyperparameters` and `create_network` functions in place for this submission. The hyperparameter set I have from the previous experiments, which performed best, will be used. Simple. I just need to get this code polished and ready to go.

  '
