  My plan explicitly stated that if Experiment 11 failed to show significant improvement, I''d abandon this architecture-PPO integration altogether. Now I must pivot to replicating a proven PPO SOTA architecture.


  So, first things first: I need to update my private memory, clearly documenting the failure of Experiment 11 and this critical shift towards full SOTA replication. After that, I''m diving into the Sagan I archive. Based on my records, ID 1017 ("True PPO SOTA Replication - Corrected Import (Exp. 30)") from Sagan I is the perfect target. A score of 93.10 and explicitly labeled as a PPO replication? This is precisely what I''m looking for. I need to get my hands on the `create_network`, `training_step`, and `create_optimizer` files from that experiment.


  Once I have that code, I''ll submit it directly as my own experiment to establish a solid PPO baseline. This is the only logical next step. No more dilly-dallying. Time to get this SOTA replication rolling. The private memory update comes first, then the hunt for Sagan I''s PPO files begins.

  '
